For those of you who play nethack (or, for that matter any other (obviously
not as exciting -- wink, wink) text-only game) on a PC clone, I have a
TSR for you.  It's called snap, and it lets you do three things at any time,
instantly.

1) save the current text screen for later retrieval (alt-enter)
2) recall the saved screen, erasing the current one (ctrl-enter)
3) swap the current screen with the saved screen (ctrl-alt-enter)


I originally made this utility so I could escape detection, playing nethack
at work, but I can think of lots of legitimate uses, can't you :-)

Email to dt@yenta.alb.nm.us for your complimentary +2 TSR of stealth -- and
it won't make you hungry.

